From 5dbf0b7994163cc0ce685db62d78916809a06605 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rinehart <johnrichardrinehart@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:06:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the device's current mode on startup

impala switched the device to `mode` (default "station") every time it
started. Opening it while an access point was running therefore
stopped the access point, and opening it in the other mode than the
device was in sat through a mode change before the first frame.

Make `mode` optional, in the config and on the command line. When it
is unset, impala opens in whatever mode the device is already in, i.e.
the one last selected. When it is set, impala only switches if the
device is in the other mode, and re-reads the device afterwards so the
UI reflects the new mode rather than the old one.
